70	// infractionOffsetDateTimeRe approximates zod v4 `z.string().datetime({ offset:
71	// true })`: a date + time (any fractional precision) followed by EITHER a literal
72	// `Z` OR a `±HH:MM` UTC offset. This is the deliberate contrast with the
73	// giveaways / kpis regexes (which end in a hard `Z$`). The dashboard/module send
74	// `.toISOString()` (UTC `Z`) values, so the valid path is exact; the error path
75	// degrades to `Invalid ISO datetime`.
